From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] stress-gpu: retry gbm surface without GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR

The Arm Mali GBM backend ("armsoc") used on NXP i.MX 95 reports
ARGB8888 as supported for LINEAR | SCANOUT | RENDERING but cannot create
a linear surface, so the gpu stressor always skipped with "could not
create gbm surface". The stressor renders off-screen and does not need a
linear buffer: retry with SCANOUT | RENDERING when the first attempt
fails.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 stress-gpu.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/stress-gpu.c b/stress-gpu.c
--- a/stress-gpu.c
+++ b/stress-gpu.c
@@ -459,6 +459,14 @@
 	gs = gbm_surface_create(gbm, size_x, size_y, GBM_BO_FORMAT_ARGB8888,
 				GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR | GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT |
 				GBM_BO_USE_RENDERING);
+	/*
+	 * Some GBM backends (e.g. the Arm Mali "armsoc" GBM on NXP i.MX 95)
+	 * cannot allocate a linear surface; the stressor renders off-screen
+	 * and does not need one, so retry without GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR.
+	 */
+	if (!gs)
+		gs = gbm_surface_create(gbm, size_x, size_y, GBM_BO_FORMAT_ARGB8888,
+					GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT | GBM_BO_USE_RENDERING);
 	if (!gs) {
 		pr_inf_skip("%s: could not create gbm surface, skipping stressor\n", args->name);
 		return EXIT_NO_RESOURCE;
-- 
